++++++++++index 000000000..df35cc33b
++++++++++--- /dev/null
+++++++++++++ b/fleet-patches/0003-common-guard-checkpoint-update_dft-against-an-empty-.patch
++++++++++@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+++++++++++From b74b2e31c1eb5a2133e1ae9c326f2b8e7bede114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+++++++++++From: Doug Gabehart <dgabehar@gmail.com>
+++++++++++Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 20:53:47 -0500
+++++++++++Subject: [PATCH] common: guard checkpoint update_dft against an empty draft
+++++++++++ sequence
+++++++++++
+++++++++++SIGSEGV / GGML_ASSERT("tensor not allocated") crash in create_checkpoint
+++++++++++-> update_dft, taking down the whole llama-server process, under
+++++++++++`--parallel>1` + draft-mtp (or any speculative type). Found live while
+++++++++++root-causing a --parallel N-slot collapse rollout crash.
+++++++++++
+++++++++++REPRODUCTION: single request, no concurrent traffic, long prompt (>16K
+++++++++++tokens, crossing the second `checkpoint_min_step` boundary at
+++++++++++2*8192=16384) sent to a fresh, previously-idle slot under `--parallel 3`.
+++++++++++Crashed mid PROMPT PROCESSING (prefill), before any token generation
+++++++++++began:
+++++++++++
+++++++++++  I slot print_timing: id  2 | task 0 | prompt processing, n_tokens = 16477
+++++++++++  D slot   operator(): id  2 | task 0 | main/do_checkpoint = yes, pos_min = 16476, pos_max = 16476
+++++++++++  /app/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp:359: GGML_ASSERT(tensor->data != NULL && "tensor not allocated") failed
+++++++++++  ... state_seq_get_data -> common_prompt_checkpoint::update_dft -> create_checkpoint ...
+++++++++++
+++++++++++ROOT CAUSE: create_checkpoint() (tools/server/server-context.cpp)
+++++++++++unconditionally calls common_prompt_checkpoint::update_dft(ctx_dft,
+++++++++++slot.id, ...) whenever a checkpoint is created -- including one triggered
+++++++++++by the periodic checkpoint_min_step threshold during PURE PROMPT PREFILL,
+++++++++++before the draft/speculative model has ever performed a forward pass for
+++++++++++that slot's sequence (draft-mtp, like every speculative type, only runs
+++++++++++during token generation, never during prefill). update_dft then calls
+++++++++++llama_state_seq_get_data_ext on ctx_dft for that sequence unconditionally.
+++++++++++
+++++++++++Under a UNIFIED KV cache (kv_unified = true, what --parallel 1 produces),
+++++++++++the single shared backing buffer is fully allocated at context-creation
+++++++++++time regardless of write history, so reading an as-yet-unused sequence's
+++++++++++(empty but allocated) region never crashes.
+++++++++++
+++++++++++Under a SPLIT (non-unified) KV cache (kv_unified = false, what
+++++++++++--parallel>1 produces on a hybrid/linear-attention architecture like
+++++++++++Qwen3.8-27B / qwen3_5), each sequence's backing buffer is allocated
+++++++++++lazily, only once that sequence is actually used. A sequence that has
+++++++++++done real target-model prefill but has NEVER been touched by the DRAFT
+++++++++++model specifically (exactly the mid-prefill-checkpoint case above) has a
+++++++++++genuinely unallocated draft-context KV buffer for that seq_id. Reading it
+++++++++++via llama_io_write_host inside state_seq_get_data hits ggml-backend's own
+++++++++++tensor->data != NULL assert and aborts the whole process -- taking down
+++++++++++every other slot's in-flight work too, not just the one request that
+++++++++++triggered it.
+++++++++++
+++++++++++Note: this is a distinct bug from the ggml allocator's view-init issue
+++++++++++(see the following commit) -- this one is a real empty/never-touched
+++++++++++sequence being read at all; that one is a sequence whose backing view was
+++++++++++never initialized even though it had been used.
+++++++++++
+++++++++++FIX: guard update_dft with llama_memory_seq_pos_max(ctx_dft, seq_id) < 0
+++++++++++(the documented upstream API for "this sequence is empty in this
+++++++++++memory") immediately after the existing ctx == nullptr early-return. When
+++++++++++the draft context genuinely has nothing for this sequence yet, leave
+++++++++++data_dft empty and return -- exactly the same state already produced
+++++++++++today when speculative decoding is disabled entirely (ctx_dft ==
+++++++++++nullptr). common_prompt_checkpoint::load_dft already no-ops on an empty
+++++++++++data_dft, so restoring a checkpoint created in this state correctly skips
+++++++++++restoring draft state that never existed, rather than erroring.
+++++++++++
+++++++++++No upstream PR tracks this -- original work, not a vendored port. This
+++++++++++looks like a genuine, previously-unreported bug affecting anyone running
+++++++++++speculative decoding with --parallel>1 on a split/non-unified KV cache,
+++++++++++worth filing upstream separately.
+++++++++++
+++++++++++Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+++++++++++Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017R3QNP4GznFWhhf11QY18j
