+++++++++@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
++++++++++From 3c4e5bf4baac5bdb383ccd950290153d3ae08de4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++++++++++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
++++++++++Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:59:57 -0500
++++++++++Subject: [PATCH] qwen3-coder: bound xml-arg-string with until_one_of, not a
++++++++++ bare until
++++++++++
++++++++++Root cause (live-traced on gabesrv06, 2026-09-15): under MTP speculative
++++++++++decoding, the qwen3-coder tool-call template has structurally-ambiguous
++++++++++decision points where the model's own greedy pick occasionally flips
++++++++++(logit margins as low as ~0.03 observed live) toward re-emitting a
++++++++++structural tag (<parameter=.../<tool_call>/</function>) instead of the
++++++++++actual argument value. The xml-arg-string rule's bare `until("\n</parameter>\n")`
++++++++++has no escape valve, so this degenerate repetition gets silently absorbed
++++++++++as "valid" string content -- it's syntactically fine, just semantically
++++++++++wrong, and none of it happens to equal the single expected terminator.
++++++++++
++++++++++The `reasoning` rule directly above this one already guards against the
++++++++++same class of problem with until_one_of({"</think>", "<tool_call>"}) --
++++++++++this rule never got the same treatment. Fix: bound xml-arg-string's value
++++++++++with until_one_of, adding the tool-call structural tags as bail-out
++++++++++terminators alongside the real closing delimiter. Because this rule also
++++++++++compiles into the sampling grammar (gbnf_excluding_grammar), this isn't
++++++++++just a post-hoc parse fix -- it makes the grammar itself reject the model
++++++++++selecting these tokens mid-value and forces a resample, closing off the
++++++++++whole failure class regardless of what causes the initial flip (this
++++++++++fleet's MTP interaction, or anything else). Costs nothing: doesn't touch
++++++++++speculative decoding, so tool-calling requests keep full MTP speed.
++++++++++
++++++++++The same bare-until gap exists in deepseek.cpp, kimi-k3.cpp, minicpm5.cpp,
++++++++++muse-glimmer.cpp, and minimax-m3.cpp's own arg-string rules -- not fixed
++++++++++here since this fleet doesn't run those models and the bug is unconfirmed
++++++++++there; worth a follow-up sweep or an upstream report.
++++++++++
++++++++++Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5
++++++++++---
++++++++++ common/parsers/qwen3-coder.cpp | 15 ++++++++++++++-
++++++++++ 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
++++++++++
++++++++++diff --git a/common/parsers/qwen3-coder.cpp b/common/parsers/qwen3-coder.cpp
++++++++++index 8a1e52137..9553804fb 100644
